Technical
### Changed

- Update the Anthropic, coverlet.collector, and Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI dependencies to newer versions. ([#328](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/328))

### Added

- **Breaking:** Remove pull request descriptions from `changelog.json` and store complete facts, including descriptions, in the run record; read fact bases from records instead of changelog files. ([#294](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/294))
- **Breaking:** Show release facts, filtering decisions, and planned model calls in `preview` without making model calls or writing files. ([#292](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/292))
- Open each command with its command header and summarize the run outcome first, with renderings grouped under audience headings. ([#342](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/342))
- Group `doctor` checks by setup area, show each status with a symbol and word, and qualify whether warnings prevent a run. ([#341](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/341))
- Show run progress with a terminal-aware spinner, and add `--plain` to every command for plain output. ([#340](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/340))
- Quote pull request titles and descriptions between tags in prompts, neutralize embedded tags, and cut long descriptions in the prompt. ([#338](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/338))
- Stop `generate` before model calls when a release is already published, unless `--replace-published` is specified; check again before writing. ([#335](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/335))
- Have `doctor` point to the version-specific configuration template when `chartula.yaml` is missing. ([#329](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/329))
- Show each run step as it proceeds, including pull request reading, audience rendering, and checks. ([#297](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/297))
- Add `chartula doctor` to check the setup required for a run before starting one. ([#295](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/295))
- Use the text available at each fact-base depth to determine closed issue numbers, and interpret the former `title-description-and-issues` value as `title-and-description`. ([#293](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/293))
- Include direct commits without pull requests as changes, while skipping merge commits and preserving range order. ([#291](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/291))
- Add `chartula --version` to print the installed informational version before reading configuration or repository data. ([#286](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/286))
- Allow a first tag to start at the first commit, and request confirmation before reading large or first-tag ranges. ([#282](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/282))

### Fixed

- Correct the help grouping so each option appears once, and update the CLI documentation and roadmap. ([#344](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/344))
- Normalize whitespace and remove code fences when comparing rendering names with fact text, while preventing matches across facts. ([#336](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/336))
- Write a standard sentence to `CHANGELOG.md` and release notes when there is nothing for technical readers, leaving `renderings.technical` empty. ([#333](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/333))
- Use relaxed JSON escaping for `changelog.json` and the run record so characters that JSON does not require escaping remain readable. ([#332](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/332))
- Separate rendering review flags from the final entry with a blank line and a `Flagged for review:` heading. ([#331](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/331))
- Show credentials as unauthenticated in the run header when their environment variables are unset or blank. ([#330](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/330))
- Validate command-specific options before starting, suggest close matches for unknown options, and honor `-h` or `--help` after a command. ([#301](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/301))
- Append a trailing slash to GitHub API base URLs that omit one, so relative request paths resolve correctly. ([#290](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/290))
- Read `filter.excludeCategories: []` as an explicit empty list that excludes no categories. ([#289](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/289))
- Report a model answer the SDK cannot parse as unreadable, distinguishing it from failures where no response arrived. ([#288](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/288))
- Refuse to run when both `chartula.yaml` and `chartula.yml` are present, and identify both paths. ([#287](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/287))
- Check whether a token can publish before the first model call in `generate`, while leaving `preview` and `--no-publish` unaffected. ([#285](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/285))
- Clarify that `--no-publish` writes every file and omits only GitHub release notes. ([#284](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/284))

